Pi Desktop is an independent desktop shell for the Pi coding agent (@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent);
it is not affiliated with or endorsed by the Pi project.

Bundled at runtime via npm (not vendored in this repository):
  Electron (MIT), marked (MIT), DOMPurify (Apache-2.0 OR MPL-2.0), highlight.js (BSD-3-Clause).

Optional tools invoked if installed: whisper.cpp (MIT), ffmpeg (LGPL/GPL), Kokoro TTS via kokoro-onnx (Apache-2.0/MIT).
The example characters' pixel faces are generated by faces/pixel_faces.py and are part of this project.

packs/learning/skills/learn/{MISSION,RESOURCES,LEARNING-RECORD,GLOSSARY}-FORMAT.md derive from the `teach` skill in
https://github.com/mattpocock/skills, Copyright (c) 2026 Matt Pocock, MIT License
(full text: packs/learning/skills/learn/LICENSE-teach.md).
The pack's characters are fictional. Their quotes are original lines; no real person is quoted or endorses them.
